1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,880
Listen, practice, speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:19,240
Hi everyone. We are really happy that you are here with us today. My name is Emma.

3
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:23,380
And my name is Daniel. Thank you so much for joining us again. We are here to help you

4
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:26,480
learn English through simple and natural conversations.

5
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:32,760
Yes. If you enjoy learning English with us, please remember to like this video and subscribe

6
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:37,520
to our channel. It really helps us continue making more lessons like this.

7
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:42,280
Thank you so much for your support. Today, we have a very interesting topic. We are going

8
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:47,160
to talk about how to talk about your achievements and proud moments in English.

9
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:52,480
That's right. Everyone has moments when they feel proud. Maybe you finished a difficult

10
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:56,840
project, learned a new skill, or finally solved a problem.

11
00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:01,320
And sometimes these moments are small, but they still make us feel happy and confident.

12
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:06,400
Exactly. Today, we will talk about these moments and show you how to describe them in English

13
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,400
in a simple way.

14
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:12,320
First, we will start with a relaxed conversation. Then, we will share some stories about our

15
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,840
own experiences.

16
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:18,440
And during the conversation, you will hear many useful phrases you can use in your daily

17
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:19,440
life.

18
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:23,240
Sounds good. So Emma, you look very cheerful today. Something good happened?

19
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:27,200
Yes, actually. I had a small but nice success this morning.

20
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,760
Oh, really? Tell me what happened.

21
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,720
Well, you know I've been trying to wake up earlier for the past few weeks.

22
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,520
Yes, you told me about that.

23
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:36,960
You wanted to start exercising in the morning, right?

24
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:37,960
Exactly.

25
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:41,680
But every day my alarm rings and I press the snooze button.

26
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,720
I know that problem very well.

27
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,700
But today was different.

28
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,700
What happened today?

29
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:51,360
Today my alarm rang at six o'clock and I actually got up immediately.

30
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,360
Wow.

31
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,360
No snooze button?

32
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,360
No snooze button.

33
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,360
That's impressive.

34
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,360
I even went for a short walk outside.

35
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,400
whether it was cool and quiet.

36
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,560
That sounds like a perfect start to the day.

37
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,600
It really was.

38
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,440
I felt very proud of myself

39
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:07,560
because I finally kept my promise to wake up early.

40
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,960
That's a great achievement.

41
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:11,440
Sometimes small habits are the hardest to build.

42
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,280
That's true.

43
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,120
What about you?

44
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,400
Did anything good happen to you recently?

45
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,440
Actually, yes.

46
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:19,440
Yesterday, I finally fixed something in my apartment

47
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,160
that had been bothering me for months.

48
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,600
Now I'm curious.

49
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,440
What was it?

50
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:25,360
My kitchen cabinet door was loose.

51
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,520
Every time I opened it,

52
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,140
It made a strange noise.

53
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:30,560
Oh no, that sounds annoying.

54
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,400
It was.

55
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,840
And every week I told myself I will fix it this weekend.

56
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,680
But you didn't?

57
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,180
No.

58
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:38,600
I always forgot or got busy with something else.

59
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,360
So what changed yesterday?

60
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,000
Yesterday I decided to stop delaying it.

61
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,360
I watched a short video online about how to tighten the hinges.

62
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,520
That's a smart idea.

63
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,360
Then I found my toolbox and started working on it.

64
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,360
Were you nervous?

65
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:51,960
A little.

66
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,000
I was worried I might make the problem worse.

67
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,280
That happens sometimes.

68
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,800
But after about 20 minutes, I finished the job.

69
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,720
And did it work?

70
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,560
Yes.

71
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,640
The door opens and closes perfectly now.

72
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,680
No noise at all.

73
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,560
That must feel satisfying.

74
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,520
It really does.

75
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,920
Every time I open the cabinet,

76
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,240
I feel proud that I fixed it myself.

77
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,760
That's a great example of a simple success.

78
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,600
Exactly.

79
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,800
Speaking of successes,

80
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,880
I remember something from last weekend

81
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,520
that made me very happy.

82
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,680
Oh, another story?

83
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,520
I like stories.

84
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:23,360
Last weekend, I decided to try a new recipe for dinner.

85
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,820
Cooking can be risky.

86
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,060
That's true, especially for me.

87
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:29,900
Wait, are you saying you are not a great cook?

88
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:32,100
Let's just say I'm still learning.

89
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:33,220
Fair enough.

90
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:34,220
What did you try to cook?

91
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,660
I tried to make homemade vegetable soup.

92
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,060
That sounds healthy and simple.

93
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:39,140
That's what I thought.

94
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:40,660
But when I started cooking,

95
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:43,060
I realized there were many steps.

96
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,460
Like chopping vegetables?

97
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:48,220
Yes, chopping carrots, onions, potatoes, and garlic.

98
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,300
That takes time.

99
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:51,620
Then I had to cook everything slowly

100
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:53,420
so the flavors would mix together.

101
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,940
Did you follow a recipe?

102
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,380
Yes, I followed it very carefully.

103
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,980
I even measured the ingredients exactly.

104
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,100
That's very professional.

105
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,980
I wanted the soup to taste good.

106
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:04,580
So what happened in the end?

107
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,780
When the soup was ready, I tasted it

108
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,100
and it was actually delicious.

109
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:10,060
That's fantastic.

110
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:11,820
I was honestly surprised.

111
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:14,300
Sometimes surprises are the best part of cooking.

112
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,620
I even invited my neighbor to try it.

113
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:17,580
Brave move.

114
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:20,580
She said it was very tasty and asked for the recipe.

115
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,660
That's the best compliment a cook can get.

116
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:25,540
I know, I felt very proud at that moment.

117
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,300
See, cooking success is always worth celebrating.

118
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,140
What about you?

119
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,180
Do you remember a moment

120
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,380
when you felt really proud of something you did?

121
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,500
Actually, yes.

122
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,500
Something happened at work last month

123
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,740
that made me feel proud.

124
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:37,580
Tell me about it.

125
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,780
Our team had to prepare a presentation

126
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,420
for a group of new clients.

127
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,220
Presentations can be stressful.

128
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,780
Especially when you have to speak

129
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:46,340
in front of many people.

130
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:47,540
How many people were there?

131
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,500
About 20 people in the meeting room.

132
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:50,620
That's quite a crowd.

133
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:55,260
Yes, and I was responsible for explaining the main idea of our project.

134
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,380
Were you nervous?

135
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:59,420
Very nervous at first. My hands were shaking a little.

136
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:00,940
That happens to many people.

137
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:03,020
But I prepared a lot before the meeting.

138
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:03,980
How did you prepare?

139
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:07,660
I wrote down the important points and practiced speaking at home.

140
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:09,420
Did you practice out loud?

141
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:15,100
Yes, I practiced several times. I even timed myself to make sure I didn't speak too long.

142
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,780
That's excellent preparation.

143
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:21,420
When the meeting started, I took a deep breath and began speaking slowly.

144
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,220
Good strategy.

145
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:25,580
As I continued talking, I started feeling more confident.

146
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,100
That's usually how it works.

147
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:31,420
By the end of the presentation, the clients were smiling and asking questions.

148
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,700
That's always a good sign.

149
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:35,420
After the meeting, my manager came to me and said,

150
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:38,700
Great job today. Your explanation was very clear.

151
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,380
That must have felt amazing.

152
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:43,180
It really did. All the practice paid off.

153
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:45,260
That's a wonderful professional success.

154
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:50,220
Yes, and it also helped me feel more confident speaking English at work.

155
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,980
Confidence grows with every success.

156
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:52,980
Exactly.

157
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,620
You know, I think many people forget to celebrate these moments.

158
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,100
That's true.

159
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:00,060
Sometimes we only focus on our mistakes.

160
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:02,980
But it's important to notice our progress, too.

161
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:03,980
Absolutely.

162
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,540
Even small achievements matter.

163
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,900
Like learning a new word in English.

164
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,560
Or understanding a movie without subtitles.

165
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,540
Or finishing a book in English.

166
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,220
All of these are real successes.

167
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:17,320
I remember when I first started learning Spanish.

168
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:17,820
Oh yes?

169
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:22,720
The first time I ordered food in Spanish at a restaurant, I felt very proud.

170
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,820
That's a big moment for language learners.

171
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,920
The waiter understood me perfectly.

172
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,120
That must have felt great.

173
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:31,920
It did. I felt like all my studying was finally useful.

174
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:34,020
Moments like that make learning fun.

175
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:34,920
Exactly.

176
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,320
Another success I remember is when I started running regularly.

177
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,120
Oh yes, your running routine.

178
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:43,020
At the beginning, I could only run for five minutes.

179
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,580
That's normal for beginners.

180
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:46,620
But after a few weeks of practice,

181
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,020
I ran for 20 minutes without stopping.

182
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:50,780
That's impressive progress.

183
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:53,020
I felt very proud of myself that day.

184
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,580
Fitness achievements are very motivating.

185
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:56,460
They really are.

186
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:59,220
I think the important lesson is that success

187
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:01,540
doesn't always mean something huge.

188
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:02,260
Exactly.

189
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:03,620
Success can be personal.

190
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:05,460
It depends on your own goals.

191
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:08,060
If your goal is to read 10 pages of a book,

192
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,260
finishing those pages is success.

193
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:14,780
If your goal is to speak English for five minutes, doing it is success.

194
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:17,100
And every small step helps you improve.

195
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,900
That's the beauty of progress.

196
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:22,740
Speaking of progress, I recently started learning how to play the piano.

197
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:23,380
Really?

198
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:24,260
That's exciting.

199
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:26,340
Yes, but it's not easy.

200
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,460
Learning an instrument takes patience.

201
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:31,780
Last week, I finally played my first full song.

202
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:32,900
That's wonderful.

203
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,740
It's a simple song, but I played it from beginning to end.

204
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,300
That's a great milestone.

205
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:40,220
My fingers made a few mistakes, but I still finished it.

206
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,420
And that's what matters.

207
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:43,800
When I finished playing, I felt very proud.

208
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,800
You should be.

209
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:47,700
My sister even recorded a short video while I was playing.

210
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:48,700
That's a nice memory.

211
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:52,260
Yes, and now I feel motivated to keep practicing.

212
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,500
Success often creates more motivation.

213
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,500
Exactly.

214
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:58,940
Another thing people sometimes forget is how to accept compliments.

215
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:00,260
That's a good point.

216
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:04,580
When someone says, good job, many people say, oh, it was nothing.

217
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:07,100
But it's okay to simply say, thank you.

218
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:11,100
Yes. Accepting compliments politely is part of communication.

219
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,100
And it shows confidence.

220
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,100
Let's imagine a short situation.

221
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:15,100
Okay.

222
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,100
I'll start. Daniel, your presentation yesterday was excellent.

223
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:20,100
Thank you. I worked hard on it.

224
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,100
Perfect response.

225
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,100
Simple and polite.

226
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,100
Exactly.

227
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,100
Positive conversations like this make workplaces friendlier.

228
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:31,100
They do. You know, sometimes success also comes from teamwork.

229
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:36,100
That's very true. Last year, my team worked on a long project together.

230
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:40,620
take many months? Yes, almost six months. That's a long time.

231
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:43,820
But when we finally finished the project, everyone felt proud.

232
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:48,980
I can imagine the feeling of relief. We celebrated with a small team dinner.

233
00:08:48,980 --> 00:08:53,460
Celebrations are important after hard work. They remind us of what we achieved together.

234
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:56,320
Exactly. Emma, do you think talking about success

235
00:08:56,320 --> 00:09:01,660
helps people feel more motivated? Definitely. When we share positive experiences,

236
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:04,980
it inspires others. And it also reminds us that progress

237
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:05,980
is possible.

238
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,580
That's a wonderful message.

239
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:12,580
So for everyone listening today, we want you to think about your own success this week.

240
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:15,540
It can be something small or something big.

241
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:17,200
Maybe you woke up early.

242
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,780
Maybe you helped a friend.

243
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:21,380
Maybe you practiced English for ten minutes.

244
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,620
Whatever it is, remember to celebrate it.

245
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:25,460
And try describing it in English.

246
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:29,860
For example, you can say, this week I finally finished my project.

247
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:32,540
Or I managed to solve a problem at work.

248
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:35,340
Or, I learned five new English words.

249
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:37,980
These simple sentences help you practice speaking.

250
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:40,460
And they also remind you of your progress.

251
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:42,340
Learning a language is a journey.

252
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,780
Every small step forward is important.

253
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:45,780
Exactly.

254
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:49,540
Before we finish today's conversation, we want to ask you a question.

255
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,480
Yes, our question for you is very simple.

256
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,180
What is one thing you succeeded in this week?

257
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,700
It can be anything at all.

258
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:58,220
Maybe you woke up everly.

259
00:09:58,220 --> 00:09:59,560
Maybe you helped a friend.

260
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,020
Maybe you practiced English for ten minutes.

261
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:04,900
Write your answer in the comments and share your success story.

262
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,680
We love reading your messages.

263
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,180
They inspire us and other learners, too.

264
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:11,500
Thank you again for spending time with us today.

265
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:15,020
Keep practicing, keep learning, and keep believing in your progress.

266
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:19,380
Remember, every success, big or small, is a step forward.

267
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,940
See you in the next conversation.

268
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:21,940
Goodbye, everyone.

269
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:23,660
Take care and keep learning English.

270
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:24,700
Hi, everyone.

271
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,500
We are really happy you are here with us today.

272
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,140
My name is Olivia.

273
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,700
And my name is Daniel.

274
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:35,060
Welcome back to our Simple English Conversation podcast where we help you learn English through

275
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:37,540
friendly and natural conversations.

276
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:42,500
If you enjoy learning English with us, please remember to like this video and subscribe to

277
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,580
our channel.

278
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:47,020
It really helps us continue making more lessons for you.

279
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:49,140
Thank you so much for your support.

280
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:52,540
Today we have another interesting and useful conversation for you.

281
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,540
Yes!

282
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:57,900
Today we are going to talk about something that everyone experiences in life.

283
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:58,900
That's right.

284
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:03,340
We are going to talk about how to talk about learning something new in English.

285
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:08,840
Learning something new can be exciting, but sometimes it can also be difficult.

286
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,840
Very true.

287
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:14,640
When we learn something new, we usually make mistakes, we practice a lot, and slowly we

288
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,740
improve.

289
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:20,420
And today, we will show you how to talk about that process in simple English.

290
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:21,420
Exactly.

291
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:25,120
We'll start with a short conversation, and then we will tell a longer story about

292
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,700
trying something new.

293
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:31,540
After that, we will share some everyday examples that you can use in your own conversations.

294
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,540
Are you ready?

295
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:33,540
Let's begin.

296
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:35,980
Olivia, you look very excited today.

297
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,180
I am excited.

298
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:39,180
I tried something new this week.

299
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,180
Really?

300
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:41,180
What did you try?

301
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:43,300
I started learning how to cook a new dish.

302
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,980
Oh, that sounds interesting.

303
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,980
What kind of dish?

304
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:50,020
I tried to cook homemade pasta for the first time.

305
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:51,260
Homemade pasta?

306
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,420
That sounds difficult.

307
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,420
Yes.

308
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,500
At first, I thought it would be easy.

309
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,180
Let me guess, it was not easy.

310
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,180
Not at all.

311
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,180
Tell me what happened.

312
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:03,260
Well, I watched a cooking video online.

313
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:06,040
The chef made it look very simple.

314
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,700
That always happens.

315
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:13,820
Yes, in the video, the chef mixed flour and eggs, and in five minutes the dough looked

316
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:15,120
perfect.

317
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:17,860
But in real life, things are different.

318
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:18,960
Exactly.

319
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:24,120
When I started mixing the flour and eggs, everything became messy.

320
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,320
Messy how?

321
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,940
The flower went everywhere.

322
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:32,040
It was on the table, on my hands, and even on the floor.

323
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:33,380
Oh no!

324
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:36,680
My kitchen looked like a small snowstorm.

325
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:38,020
That sounds funny.

326
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:42,140
It was funny later, but at the time I was a little stressed.

327
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,940
Did you think about giving up?

328
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:45,480
For a moment, yes.

329
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,460
But then I said to myself, no, I want to learn this.

330
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,100
That is a good attitude.

331
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:54,260
So I cleaned the table and tried again.

332
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:55,900
And did it work the second time?

333
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,900
It was better, but still not perfect.

334
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,020
What was the problem?

335
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:02,460
The dough was too sticky.

336
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:03,540
So what did you do?

337
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:05,300
I added more flour.

338
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,180
That sounds reasonable.

339
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:09,740
Then the dough became too dry.

340
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:12,460
Cooking is like a science experiment sometimes.

341
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,620
Yes, it really is.

342
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:15,940
So what happened next?

343
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:18,940
I decided to relax and take my time.

344
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:19,940
Good idea.

345
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:24,260
Slowly mix the dough and followed the recipe step by step.

346
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:25,580
And finally?

347
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:28,940
Finally, the dough looked smooth and soft.

348
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:30,380
That must have felt good.

349
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,340
It did.

350
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:33,700
I felt like a real chef for a moment.

351
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,420
So the pasta was ready?

352
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,420
Not yet.

353
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:37,620
There's more?

354
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:38,620
Yes.

355
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:42,540
After making the dough, I had to roll it very thin.

356
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:43,900
That sounds tricky.

357
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:44,900
It was.

358
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:48,740
I used a rolling pin, but the dough kept moving around.

359
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,540
That must have been frustrating.

360
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:53,100
A little bit, but I kept practicing.

361
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,860
Practice makes progress.

362
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:56,380
Exactly.

363
00:13:56,380 --> 00:14:00,100
After some time, the pasta sheets finally looked right.

364
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,300
So you cut them into pasta noodles?

365
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,900
Yes, long, thin noodles.

366
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:06,140
And then you cooked them?

367
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:09,620
Yes, I boiled them in hot water for a few minutes.

368
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:12,300
Now comes the most important question.

369
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,300
I know what you're going to ask.

370
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,260
Did it taste good?

371
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:17,980
Surprisingly, yes.

372
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:18,980
That's great!

373
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:22,940
It was not perfect, but it tasted fresh and delicious.

374
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,580
That must have been a proud moment.

375
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,860
I felt very proud.

376
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:29,740
Learning something new always feels good when it works.

377
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:32,260
Yes, even if it takes time.

378
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:36,180
Speaking of learning new things, I also tried something new recently.

379
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,180
Really?

380
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,180
What did you try?

381
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:40,660
I started learning how to ride a bicycle again.

382
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:41,660
Again?

383
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,660
Yes.

384
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:45,860
I learned as a child, but I didn't ride for many years.

385
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,860
So you forgot how to do it?

386
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:51,300
not completely, but I felt very nervous.

387
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,540
That makes sense.

388
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:55,020
Last weekend I rented a bicycle at the park.

389
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,020
Were you scared?

390
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,300
A little.

391
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:59,020
What was the hardest part?

392
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,580
Keeping my balance.

393
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,740
That is always the tricky part.

394
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,440
At first I rode very slowly.

395
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,860
Did anyone see you?

396
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,700
Yes, many people were riding bicycles.

397
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,620
Did you feel embarrassed?

398
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:14,900
Just a little, but then I remembered something important.

399
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,300
What was that?

400
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,060
starts somewhere.

401
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,420
That's a good way to think.

402
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,260
So I continued practicing.

403
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,460
Did it get easier?

404
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:23,460
Yes.

405
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:26,500
After about 20 minutes, I started feeling more comfortable.

406
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,900
That's great.

407
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:30,500
Soon I was riding smoothly around the park.

408
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,620
That sounds like real progress.

409
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:33,620
It was.

410
00:15:33,620 --> 00:15:36,340
The wind was blowing and the sun was shining.

411
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,980
That sounds like a beautiful moment.

412
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:40,540
It really was.

413
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:43,820
Learning something new can bring simple happiness.

414
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:44,820
Exactly.

415
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:47,500
So how long did you ride the bicycle?

416
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,500
Almost an hour.

417
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,460
Wow, that's impressive!

418
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:53,500
At the end, I felt tired but very happy.

419
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,140
Did you plan to ride again?

420
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,140
Definitely.

421
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:59,740
What I like about your story is that you didn't give up.

422
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:01,900
That's important when learning anything.

423
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:02,900
Yes.

424
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:07,180
Whether it's cooking, riding a bicycle, or learning English.

425
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:11,740
Speaking of English, many people feel nervous when they start speaking.

426
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:12,740
That's true.

427
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,380
The only way to improve is to practice.

428
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:16,900
Exactly.

429
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:18,780
Mistakes are part of learning.

430
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:22,660
Let's imagine a few situations where people learn something new.

431
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,780
Good idea.

432
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:26,860
First situation, learning a musical instrument.

433
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,860
Okay.

434
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:28,860
I'll start.

435
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:29,860
Go ahead.

436
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:30,860
Hey, Daniel.

437
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,020
What are you doing with that guitar?

438
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:34,060
I'm trying to learn a new song.

439
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,060
How is it going?

440
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,060
Slowly, but I'm improving.

441
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:38,140
That's great.

442
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:41,020
At first, my fingers hurt a lot.

443
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:43,300
That happens when you start playing guitar.

444
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,100
But I practiced every day.

445
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:46,100
And now?

446
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,140
Now I can play the whole chorus.

447
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,100
That's wonderful progress.

448
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,100
Thank you.

449
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:53,700
Now let's imagine another situation.

450
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:55,060
What situation?

451
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,500
Learning a new language.

452
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,500
Perfect.

453
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:00,140
Hi Daniel, how's your English study going?

454
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,300
It's getting better.

455
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,700
What helped you improve?

456
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:05,620
I started listening to podcasts every day.

457
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:07,020
That's a great habit.

458
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,420
At first I understood only a little.

459
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,500
That is normal.

460
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,860
But now I understand much more.

461
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,060
That's real progress.

462
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:16,900
Yes, and I feel more confident.

463
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:19,780
Confidence is very important when learning a language.

464
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:20,780
Definitely.

465
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:23,540
Let's imagine another everyday situation.

466
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,540
Okay.

467
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:26,260
Learning how to drive.

468
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:27,780
That can be stressful.

469
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:29,340
But also exciting.

470
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:30,460
I'll start this one.

471
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,460
Go ahead.

472
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:32,460
Hi, Olivia.

473
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:33,460
Guess what?

474
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:34,460
What happened?

475
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:36,500
I had my first driving lesson today.

476
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:37,500
Really?

477
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,500
How was it?

478
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,940
I was very nervous at the beginning.

479
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:41,420
I can imagine.

480
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:43,700
But the instructor was very patient.

481
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:44,820
That helps a lot.

482
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:47,220
He explained everything slowly.

483
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:48,620
Were you able to drive?

484
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,020
Yes, a little.

485
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,020
That's great!

486
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:53,260
I practiced turning and stopping.

487
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:55,100
Those are important skills.

488
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,820
By the end of the lesson, I felt more relaxed.

489
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:00,180
That sounds like a good first step.

490
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:02,220
Yes, learning takes time.

491
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,660
But step by step, we improve.

492
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:06,100
Exactly.

493
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:09,780
Another important thing when learning something new is patience.

494
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:12,780
Sometimes people expect fast results.

495
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:15,780
But real learning takes practice and time.

496
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:17,780
Think about learning to swim.

497
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:19,780
That's a great example.

498
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:21,780
At first you might feel scared in the water.

499
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:24,780
Yes, and you may move slowly.

500
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:27,780
But after many lessons you become comfortable.

501
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,780
Eventually swimming feels natural.

502
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:32,780
The same thing happens with many skills.

503
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:35,780
Cooking, sports, music, languages.

504
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:37,780
Even simple things like gardening.

505
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:40,780
That's true. My neighbor recently started gardening.

506
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:41,780
Really?

507
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,780
Yes. At first, none of the plants grew well.

508
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:46,780
That must have been disappointing.

509
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,780
A little, but she didn't stop trying.

510
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,780
What did she do?

511
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:53,780
She read books about plants and sunlight.

512
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:54,780
Good idea.

513
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,780
She also talked to other gardeners.

514
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,780
Learning from others is very helpful.

515
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:00,780
Now her garden looks beautiful.

516
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:03,780
That is a wonderful result.

517
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:06,780
It shows that patience and effort can bring success.

518
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:09,380
I completely agree.

519
00:19:09,380 --> 00:19:13,300
When you learn something new, every small improvement is important.

520
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:17,180
Yes, small steps lead to big progress.

521
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:20,060
Sometimes people forget to celebrate small improvements.

522
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:23,140
But those small moments keep us motivated.

523
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,380
Exactly.

524
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:27,940
For example, when someone learns 10 new English words.

525
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,580
That's a great achievement.

526
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:32,680
Or when someone finishes a reading a book in English.

527
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:34,020
Another big step.

528
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:38,220
Even understanding a movie scene without subtitles is progress.

529
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,780
Absolutely.

530
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:41,740
Learning is like climbing a mountain.

531
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,020
That's a nice comparison.

532
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:46,340
You move slowly, but you keep going higher.

533
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:49,740
And when you look back, you realize how far you've come.

534
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:52,180
That feeling is very satisfying.

535
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:53,540
It really is.

536
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:59,380
So today we talked about learning new things and how to describe that experience in English.

537
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:04,540
We shared stories about cooking pasta, riding bicycles, learning guitar, and many other

538
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:05,540
activities.

539
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:08,100
The most important idea is simple.

540
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,460
Keep trying and keep practicing.

541
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,380
Mistakes are normal.

542
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,160
Progress takes time.

543
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:17,540
And learning something new can bring a lot of joy.

544
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:20,740
Before we finish today's conversation, we have a question for you.

545
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:23,820
Yes, we always enjoy reading your answers.

546
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:26,380
Our question today is very simple.

547
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:29,300
What is something new you learned recently?

548
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:31,580
Maybe you learned a new English word.

549
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:33,580
Maybe you cooked a new recipe.

550
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:35,660
Maybe you started a new hobby.

551
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:38,120
Whatever it is, we would love to hear your story.

552
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:40,660
You can write a simple sentence like this.

553
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:42,700
This week I learned how to...

554
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,740
Then tell us your experience.

555
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:47,820
Sharing your story is a great way to practice English.

556
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:50,240
And it can inspire other learners, too.

557
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:52,740
Thank you so much for spending time with us today.

558
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:56,900
We hope this conversation helped you learn new words and ideas.

559
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:59,060
Keep practicing your English every day.

560
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:03,480
And remember, learning something new is always an exciting journey.

561
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,840
From both of us, goodbye, everyone.

562
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:10,960
See you next time and keep learning.

563
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,220
Hi, everyone.

564
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,220
Welcome back.

565
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:16,120
We are really happy that you are here with us today.

566
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,120
Hello, everyone.

567
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,320
My name is Daniel.

568
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:19,760
And my name is Sarah.

569
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:24,040
We are here to help you learn English with simple and natural conversations.

570
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:27,240
Yes, conversations that feel like real life.

571
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:30,840
Nothing too difficult, just clear and friendly English.

572
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:35,940
If you enjoy learning English this way, please support us by liking this video and subscribing

573
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:37,100
to the channel.

574
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:40,460
It really helps us continue making lessons like this.

575
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:42,340
Thank you very much for your support.

576
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:45,180
So Daniel, what are we going to talk about today?

577
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,500
Today we have a very positive topic.

578
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:50,020
Oh, I like positive topics.

579
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,020
Me too.

580
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:55,220
Today we will talk about achieving goals and small personal victories.

581
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:56,860
That sounds great.

582
00:21:56,860 --> 00:21:59,420
Everyone likes the feeling of achieving something.

583
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:00,420
Exactly.

584
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:04,840
Sometimes success is something big, but many times it is something small.

585
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:08,380
Like finishing a difficult task or learning something new.

586
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:11,380
Or cooking a meal that turns out very good.

587
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:14,500
That reminds me of something that happened to me last weekend.

588
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:15,500
Really?

589
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:16,500
Now I'm curious.

590
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:20,540
Yes, I tried something new and it actually worked.

591
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:23,300
That sounds like a success story already.

592
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:26,100
Maybe a small one, but it made me happy.

593
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:27,820
Small successes are the best.

594
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:30,140
They make ordinary days special.

595
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,420
Very true.

596
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:33,420
So Sarah, tell us what happened.

597
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:37,020
Okay, last weekend I decided to try baking bread

598
00:22:37,020 --> 00:22:38,460
for the first time.

599
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:40,560
Bread, that is not easy.

600
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,080
Exactly, that's why I was nervous.

601
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:46,320
I understand, baking bread requires patience.

602
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:50,100
Yes, first I searched for a simple recipe online.

603
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:51,180
Good idea.

604
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:53,500
Then I went to the store to buy flour,

605
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:55,540
yeast, and other ingredients.

606
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,300
You were very prepared.

607
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:59,660
I wanted everything to be perfect.

608
00:22:59,660 --> 00:23:01,260
So what happened next?

609
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:05,300
When I came home, I read the recipe slowly two times.

610
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,220
That is smart.

611
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:08,100
Many people skipped that step.

612
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:10,100
I didn't want to make a mistake.

613
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:12,140
Did you start baking immediately?

614
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:12,820
Yes.

615
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:15,820
First, I mixed the warm water and yeast.

616
00:23:15,820 --> 00:23:16,900
Did it bubble?

617
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:17,660
Yes.

618
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:20,100
I was so happy when I saw the bubbles.

619
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:22,140
That means the yeast is active.

620
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:23,140
Exactly.

621
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:25,660
Then I added flour and salt.

622
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:27,820
And then you had to knead the dough.

623
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:28,420
Yes.

624
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:30,540
and that part was hard work.

625
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:32,580
Needing dough takes energy.

626
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:35,900
My arms started to feel tired after a few minutes.

627
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:37,540
But you kept going.

628
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:41,140
Yes, the recipe said knead for 10 minutes.

629
00:23:41,140 --> 00:23:44,060
10 minutes feels long when you're kneading dough.

630
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:45,540
It really does.

631
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:47,300
Did the dough become soft?

632
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:50,900
Yes, after some time it felt smooth and elastic.

633
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,460
That means you did it right.

634
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:54,420
Then I placed the dough in a bowl

635
00:23:54,420 --> 00:23:56,020
and covered it with a towel.

636
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:57,660
That is for rising.

637
00:23:57,660 --> 00:24:00,280
Yes, and I had to wait one hour.

638
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:02,320
Waiting is the hardest part.

639
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:05,320
I kept checking the bowl every few minutes.

640
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:06,840
I do the same thing.

641
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:09,760
After one hour, the dough doubled in size.

642
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:11,400
That is a good sign.

643
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,520
I felt excited at that moment.

644
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:15,320
So what did you do next?

645
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:18,600
I shaped the dough into a loaf and put it in the oven.

646
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:21,080
Did your kitchen start smelling amazing?

647
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:25,360
Yes, the smell of fresh bread filled the whole room.

648
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:28,080
That is one of the best smells in the world.

649
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,120
I agree.

650
00:24:29,120 --> 00:24:32,280
So the big question, how did the bread taste?

651
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,640
Honestly, it was really good.

652
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:36,200
Congratulations.

653
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:37,040
Thank you.

654
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,700
I was so proud of myself.

655
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:40,040
You should be proud.

656
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:42,160
I even shared some with my neighbor.

657
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:43,600
And what did they say?

658
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:46,320
They said it tasted like bread from a bakery.

659
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:48,440
That is a wonderful compliment.

660
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:50,680
Yes, it made me very happy.

661
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:54,400
See, that is a perfect example of a personal success.

662
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:55,340
Exactly.

663
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:57,820
Now, I want to share my own story.

664
00:24:57,820 --> 00:24:58,780
I'm ready.

665
00:24:58,780 --> 00:25:01,460
Last week, I had a challenge at work.

666
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:02,940
What kind of challenge?

667
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:06,380
My manager asked me to present an idea to the team.

668
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:08,460
Presentations can be stressful.

669
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:10,780
Yes, especially in English.

670
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:11,980
Were you nervous?

671
00:25:11,980 --> 00:25:13,380
Very nervous.

672
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:15,100
What did you do to prepare?

673
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:17,700
First, I wrote down my main points.

674
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:18,940
Good strategy.

675
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:21,340
Then I practiced speaking at home.

676
00:25:21,340 --> 00:25:22,220
Out loud?

677
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:23,620
Yes, out loud.

678
00:25:23,620 --> 00:25:25,060
That helps a lot.

679
00:25:25,060 --> 00:25:27,240
I practiced in front of the mirror.

680
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,680
That takes courage.

681
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:30,840
It felt strange at first.

682
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:32,200
But useful.

683
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,360
Very useful.

684
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:35,160
Did you also record yourself?

685
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:38,800
Yes, I used my phone to record the presentation.

686
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:41,080
Listening to your own voice can be surprising.

687
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:43,600
Yes, but it helped me notice my mistakes.

688
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:45,720
That's a great learning method.

689
00:25:45,720 --> 00:25:48,920
I practiced every evening for three days.

690
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,440
That is real dedication.

691
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:53,120
Finally, the day of the meeting arrived.

692
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:54,720
How did you feel that morning?

693
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,820
My heart was beating fast.

694
00:25:56,820 --> 00:25:58,320
That happens to everyone.

695
00:25:58,320 --> 00:26:01,220
I took a deep breath and started speaking.

696
00:26:01,220 --> 00:26:02,940
Did the words come easily?

697
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:05,300
At first, I was a little slow.

698
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:06,300
That's okay.

699
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:09,500
But after a few minutes, I felt more confident.

700
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:11,300
Confidence grows while speaking.

701
00:26:11,300 --> 00:26:12,300
Exactly.

702
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:14,300
Did your team understand your idea?

703
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:15,940
Yes, they listened carefully.

704
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:17,620
That's a good sign.

705
00:26:17,620 --> 00:26:20,500
At the end, my manager said something nice.

706
00:26:20,500 --> 00:26:21,580
What did she say?

707
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:25,300
She said, that was a clear and helpful presentation.

708
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:27,020
That must have felt great.

709
00:26:27,020 --> 00:26:28,340
It really did.

710
00:26:28,340 --> 00:26:30,180
Did the team like your idea?

711
00:26:30,180 --> 00:26:32,660
Yes, they decided to try it next month.

712
00:26:32,660 --> 00:26:34,340
That's a big success.

713
00:26:34,340 --> 00:26:36,780
I felt proud and relieved.

714
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:38,660
Your hard work paid off.

715
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:39,660
Exactly.

716
00:26:39,660 --> 00:26:42,660
I noticed something interesting about our stories.

717
00:26:42,660 --> 00:26:43,660
What is that?

718
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:45,940
Both stories have the same pattern.

719
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:46,940
You're right.

720
00:26:46,940 --> 00:26:48,500
First, we had a goal.

721
00:26:48,500 --> 00:26:49,500
Yes.

722
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:50,940
Then, we prepared.

723
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:53,020
After that, we worked hard.

724
00:26:53,020 --> 00:26:55,280
And finally, we succeeded.

725
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,420
That is the recipe for success.

726
00:26:57,420 --> 00:27:01,020
Goal, preparation, effort, and result.

727
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:03,540
Very simple but very powerful.

728
00:27:03,540 --> 00:27:06,660
Let's talk about some smaller everyday successes.

729
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:07,660
Good idea.

730
00:27:07,660 --> 00:27:10,540
For example, learning new English words.

731
00:27:10,540 --> 00:27:13,380
That is a common goal for many learners.

732
00:27:13,380 --> 00:27:14,860
Imagine this situation.

733
00:27:14,860 --> 00:27:15,860
Okay.

734
00:27:15,860 --> 00:27:17,660
I meet you after class.

735
00:27:17,660 --> 00:27:18,660
Let's try it.

736
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:21,160
Hey Daniel, how was your English class today?

737
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:22,660
It was great, actually.

738
00:27:22,660 --> 00:27:23,660
Really?

739
00:27:23,660 --> 00:27:24,660
Why?

740
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:26,780
Today I understood the whole lesson.

741
00:27:26,780 --> 00:27:27,780
That's wonderful.

742
00:27:27,780 --> 00:27:30,580
Even the listening exercise was easy for me.

743
00:27:30,580 --> 00:27:32,060
That shows your progress.

744
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:35,320
Yes, I feel like my English is improving.

745
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:36,940
That must feel rewarding.

746
00:27:36,940 --> 00:27:37,940
It does.

747
00:27:37,940 --> 00:27:40,580
Now let's imagine another situation.

748
00:27:40,580 --> 00:27:41,740
Okay.

749
00:27:41,740 --> 00:27:43,580
Imagine a personal fitness school.

750
00:27:43,580 --> 00:27:45,140
I like that.

751
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:46,740
Imagine we meet in the park.

752
00:27:46,740 --> 00:27:47,740
Ready.

753
00:27:47,740 --> 00:27:49,620
Daniel, you look tired.

754
00:27:49,620 --> 00:27:51,860
I just finished a long run.

755
00:27:51,860 --> 00:27:53,300
How far did you run?

756
00:27:53,300 --> 00:27:55,740
I ran five kilometers today.

757
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:57,140
That's impressive.

758
00:27:57,140 --> 00:28:00,020
Last month I could only run two kilometers.

759
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:01,380
That's big progress.

760
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:04,100
I trained a little every day.

761
00:28:04,100 --> 00:28:05,100
Consistency is important.

762
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:08,700
Yes, and today I finally reached my goal.

763
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:09,700
Well done.

764
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:10,700
Thank you.

765
00:28:10,700 --> 00:28:13,420
Now let's talk about another kind of success.

766
00:28:13,420 --> 00:28:14,420
What kind?

767
00:28:14,420 --> 00:28:15,700
Helping someone.

768
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:17,620
That is a beautiful kind of success.

769
00:28:17,620 --> 00:28:21,700
Yes. Yesterday I helped my friend move into a new apartment.

770
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,460
Moving can be stressful.

771
00:28:23,460 --> 00:28:25,220
It was a lot of work.

772
00:28:25,220 --> 00:28:26,340
What did you do?

773
00:28:26,340 --> 00:28:29,220
I helped carry boxes and organized furniture.

774
00:28:29,220 --> 00:28:30,820
That sounds exhausting.

775
00:28:30,820 --> 00:28:33,620
It was, but my friend was very grateful.

776
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:35,060
That must feel good.

777
00:28:35,060 --> 00:28:37,860
Yes. Helping someone makes me feel proud.

778
00:28:37,860 --> 00:28:40,020
Kindness is a success too.

779
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:43,540
Absolutely. Let's talk about another situation.

780
00:28:43,540 --> 00:28:44,260
Sure.

781
00:28:44,260 --> 00:28:47,700
Imagine someone finally fixes something in their house.

782
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:49,860
Like repairing a broken chair.

783
00:28:49,860 --> 00:28:50,820
Exactly.

784
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:52,660
That happened to me last month.

785
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:53,460
Really?

786
00:28:53,460 --> 00:28:56,980
My desk was shaking every time I used my laptop.

787
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:58,580
That sounds annoying.

788
00:28:58,580 --> 00:28:59,620
It was.

789
00:28:59,620 --> 00:29:00,740
What did you do?

790
00:29:00,740 --> 00:29:03,060
I watched a few tutorial videos.

791
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:04,260
Good solution.

792
00:29:04,260 --> 00:29:07,300
Then I used a screwdriver to tighten the screws.

793
00:29:07,300 --> 00:29:08,340
Did it work?

794
00:29:08,340 --> 00:29:11,140
Yes, the desk is completely stable now.

795
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:12,180
That's great.

796
00:29:12,180 --> 00:29:14,980
It was a small victory, but it made me happy.

797
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:17,380
Small victories give us confidence.

798
00:29:17,380 --> 00:29:18,480
Exactly.

799
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:22,080
Now another interesting success is learning a new skill.

800
00:29:22,080 --> 00:29:24,180
Like playing a musical instrument?

801
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:27,680
Yes, I actually started learning the guitar recently.

802
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:28,980
That's exciting.

803
00:29:28,980 --> 00:29:31,080
At first, my fingers hurt.

804
00:29:31,080 --> 00:29:32,980
That happens to every beginner.

805
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:36,580
But after some practice, I learned my first full song.

806
00:29:36,580 --> 00:29:38,080
Congratulations!

807
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:39,580
It felt amazing.

808
00:29:39,580 --> 00:29:42,220
Music progress is very rewarding.

809
00:29:42,220 --> 00:29:43,180
I agree.

810
00:29:43,180 --> 00:29:45,740
Now, let's talk about something important.

811
00:29:45,740 --> 00:29:46,540
What is it?

812
00:29:46,540 --> 00:29:50,060
Sometimes people feel shy talking about their successes.

813
00:29:50,060 --> 00:29:51,100
That's true.

814
00:29:51,100 --> 00:29:53,420
They say things like it was nothing.

815
00:29:53,420 --> 00:29:55,740
Yes, they don't want to seem proud.

816
00:29:55,740 --> 00:29:58,060
But it's okay to share good news.

817
00:29:58,060 --> 00:29:58,940
Exactly.

818
00:29:58,940 --> 00:30:01,420
You can share success without bragging.

819
00:30:01,420 --> 00:30:03,420
Just be honest and grateful.

820
00:30:03,420 --> 00:30:07,100
And when someone tells you their success, you can encourage them.

821
00:30:07,100 --> 00:30:08,780
For example, you can say,

822
00:30:08,780 --> 00:30:09,740
Well done!

823
00:30:09,740 --> 00:30:11,500
Or, I'm happy for you.

824
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:13,340
Or, that's amazing!

825
00:30:13,340 --> 00:30:16,300
These words create positive conversations.

826
00:30:16,300 --> 00:30:18,300
Positivity is powerful.

827
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:21,420
It also motivates people to continue improving.

828
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:22,460
Very true.

829
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:26,300
Before we finish, let's review a few useful expressions.

830
00:30:26,300 --> 00:30:27,340
Good idea.

831
00:30:27,340 --> 00:30:29,740
First expression, I did it.

832
00:30:29,740 --> 00:30:31,740
